; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; common.vla - a library of template macros that a cartridge's source includes
; (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8), 0BSD with the cartridges, so it is copied freely. The pass
; knows none of these by name: each is a text an author wrote, and a source may define
; its own beside them, or include a library of its own instead. They are examples, to
; be read, copied, changed and outgrown. Since KIT.1 they hold the kit's first verbs,
; the patterns two cartridges wrote alike by hand, or one wrote as the page spells it;
; since KIT.2 the picture, a string a row of cells and a character a cell; since CART.4,
; the stacking game Kairos, the verbs every and since, the look map, a still Camera and
; the Write sheet's row; since ENGINE.9 interior, the rule over a board's interior,
; whose size a source states once, as a parameter a door may give another value; since
; KIT.5 the verbs take expressions, the language's formula syntax writing each row's
; text, so that a formula is composed from forms and named macros and no longer fused
; from texts; since KIT.6 within and priority, a test of two bounds and a choice by
; the first test that holds, so that a choice of five reads as five lines; and since
; KIT.6's second slice its lists are loops, and put takes its pieces by name, so that a
; call says what each part is and not where it stands; and since its third slice a cell
; has a name, a block's labels and its words from one list, and a verb writes its row at
; a name, so that a formula reads as what it means and not where its cells are; and
; since vla-lang 0.14.0, Frazaro's VLA.16, a loop names an entry's parts, so that a
; template reads aloud as what it does.
;
; The rules each macro here keeps, which are the language's:
;   - Template macros only. A parameter is replaced by the form the caller passes; no
;     gensym and no eval, every binding named by the caller.
;   - A parameter never takes the name of a row it writes: a parameter called name
;     would replace the head of a (name ...) row too, and the load would refuse the row.
;     Nor, since KIT.5, the name of a function a formula calls, row or sum, where the
;     macro's own body calls it: the parameter would replace that head too.
;   - A list is a loop (vla-lang 0.12.0, Frazaro's VLA.5): (each (entry entries) form)
;     writes its forms once an element, and (each-index (row text texts top) form) with
;     a count beside each element, from the start the macro names, since a sheet's rows
;     count from 1 and the Palette from 0. A loop is one application and no chain, so a
;     call holds as many entries as its sheet does. Standing alone a loop writes one
;     begin; as an element of a list it is spliced there, (+ (each (n sites) n)) a sum.
;     A loop refuses a name its template already holds, and a list written as a macro's
;     call, which no primitive expands: a list a macro makes is handed on, (then (a b)),
;     as Superposition's neighbors hands its eight.
;   - An entry's parts are named in its loop (vla-lang 0.14.0, Frazaro's VLA.16): (each
;     ((address value) entries) form) binds address and value to each entry's two parts,
;     and (each-index (index (color name) entries 0) form) the same beside a count. An
;     entry of another size is refused by name, vla-each-entry-shape, the entry shown,
;     and each name is checked as a loop's name is. A list of no fixed shape is read by
;     its head and the rest still, car and cdr, as on, at and priority read theirs, and
;     so is one entry no loop walks: a name's pair, a device's entry and a legend's.
;   - A walk is kept only where a macro writes a nest, as priority does below. A
;     reference's first cell and its twin are the language's, first-cell-expand and last
;     (Frazaro's VLA.15 and VLA.6), so no macro walks a text's characters. A chain stops
;     at 5,000 links: each application is one, and so is each begin it unwraps.
;   - A macro that writes a nest recurses inside the form it writes, a level a step:
;     priority's (if test value (priority rest...)). A form nests at most 64 lists deep,
;     the language's limit, so a rule's priority holds at most 61 clauses and an else,
;     as the same IFs written by hand do (measured, KIT.6).
;   - A piece named in the call is a parameter declared after the positional ones:
;     (defmacro (put write-sheet at (sheet) (when) (address) (value)) ...) takes (sheet
;     "Tower") and the rest in any order (vla-lang 0.13.0, Frazaro's VLA.9). A piece
;     left out, given twice, unknown or holding two forms is refused by name at the
;     call's line.
;   - An address is joined: (&expand "A" (+expand index 1)) is the text "A1", since
;     &expand joins its atoms into one text and +expand adds two numbers as the macro
;     expands. A column is reached by arithmetic too, (address-expand row column) or
;     (column-letters-expand column), and a text is split by characters-expand: the
;     expand-time primitives vla-lang 0.9.0 added (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8).
;   - A macro's call is no argument of &expand, nor of symbol, nor of any expand-time
;     primitive, which takes its arguments as data: (&expand "=" (beside "A1" 1)) is
;     refused, with the id vla-expand-arg-is-list. The primitives nest instead, as beside's
;     own (address-expand (row-expand at) ...) does.
;   - A formula is written by the formula syntax (VLA.4, vla-lang 0.10.0): (formula-expand
;     expression) is the row's text, in Excel's own spelling, a reference bare, Input!B5
;     or Screen.last!A1:C3, a test (= State!B1 4), a sum (+ a b c), a text "x", a truth
;     value true. The syntax expands its expression first, so a macro's call stands inside
;     it, (edge Input!B13) for AND(Input!B13=1,Input.last!B13=0), and an expand-time primitive computes
;     there, (ref "Probe" (&expand "$D" row)) for Probe!$D1. A verb's pieces are such
;     expressions, and a verb inside another verb's piece is refused by name, since each
;     verb's row is a formula-expand of its own (vla-formula-expand-nested); a predicate
;     two verbs share is an expression macro, as edge is, and stands in either.
;   - A name is a word for a cell, and a verb's row may stand at one: (at stop (rule ...)),
;     by the section on names below (Frazaro's VLA.6 and VLA.15).

; ---- one sheet, named once ----------------------------------------------------------
; A run of rows on one sheet, the sheet named at the top of the run and not on every
; row: cells and formulas take entries, each an address or a range and what it holds,
; and on takes rows, or calls of a verb or a picture, each written without its sheet.
; The cartridge the pass writes still names the sheet on every row, which stands alone
; there, as the record prints it (docs/SPEC.md section 7.3).

(defmacro (cells sheet & entries)
  "Puts values in cells of one sheet. Each entry is a cell's address, or a range of cells, and the value that goes there."
  (each ((address value) entries)
    (cell sheet address value)))

(defmacro (formulas sheet & entries)
  "Puts formulas in cells of one sheet. Each entry is a cell's address, or a range of cells, and its formula's text, written out or by formula-expand."
  (each ((address text) entries)
    (formula sheet address text)))

(defmacro (on sheet & forms)
  "rows of one sheet, named once: each a row, or a call whose first argument is the sheet, written without it"
  (each (item forms)
    (cons (car item) (cons sheet (cdr item)))))

; A formula written as an expression (KIT.5): rule is the formula row with the syntax
; writing its text, (rule "Screen" "A1" (mod Clock!$B$1 16)) the row (formula "Screen"
; "A1" "=MOD(Clock!$B$1,16)"), and rules is formulas over expressions, one sheet named
; once. The formula row itself, and formulas, keep a text, for a formula pasted as Excel
; shows it or one the syntax cannot write.

(defmacro (rule sheet range expression)
  "one formula row from an expression: the formula syntax writes its text in Excel's spelling"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand expression)))

(defmacro (rules sheet & entries)
  "Puts formulas in cells of one sheet from expressions. Each entry is a cell's address, or a range of cells, and the expression its formula says."
  (each ((address expression) entries)
    (rule sheet address expression)))

; ---- the sheets, and their words ----------------------------------------------------
; A cartridge's sheets in tab order, each visible; a sheet hidden is written as its own
; row, (sheet "X" hidden). Then a sheet's own words: a block of settings holds a label
; in column A beside each value in column B, and a table holds its headers in row 1
; over its columns (docs/SPEC.md section 3). Each takes the cell its first text goes in, and
; the texts in order, a text or a number each.

(defmacro (sheets & tabs)
  "the sheets in tab order, each visible: a (sheet name visible) row a name"
  (each (tab tabs)
    (sheet tab visible)))

(defmacro (labels sheet first & texts)
  "texts down a column from a cell, one a row: a block's labels"
  (each-index (row text texts (row-expand first))
    (cell sheet (address-expand row (column-expand first)) text)))

(defmacro (headers sheet first & texts)
  "texts along a row from a cell, one a column: a table's headers"
  (each-index (column text texts (column-expand first))
    (cell sheet (address-expand (row-expand first) column) text)))

; A run of columns' widths and a run of rows' heights: a column row for each column from one
; to another, by number, each the width given and the format its empty cells draw, or none;
; and a row row for each row, each the height given in points. Superposition's lattice wrote
; the first, its sites three characters wide, 21 pixels beside the default row's 20, and
; Seiyaku both, its variables 88 pixels square; Brickwork's wall is their next client
; (CART.3), so they live here since. A column or a row is one row, so a run is one
; application a column or a row.

(defmacro (widths sheet from last width style)
  "a column row a column, from the column given to the last, each its width and its empty cells' format"
  (quote-if (>expand from last)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (column sheet (column-letters-expand from) width shown style)
      (quasiquote (widths (unquote sheet) (unquote (+expand from 1)) (unquote last) (unquote width) (unquote style))))))

(defmacro (heights sheet from last height)
  "a row row a row, from the row given to the last, each its height in points"
  (quote-if (>expand from last)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (row sheet from height shown)
      (quasiquote (heights (unquote sheet) (unquote (+expand from 1)) (unquote last) (unquote height))))))

; ---- names: a block's words, a verb's row at a word, the devices (KIT.6) ---------------
; A name is a word for a cell (Frazaro's VLA.6): a define binds it for every form after its
; own and writes no row, so that a formula says (= phase sliding) where it said (= State!B1
; 1). Its twin is (last phase), State.last!B1, and its anchored reading (absolute phase),
; State!$B$1, each the formula syntax's. A block's labels and its words come from one list:
; names writes each label in a column from the first cell down and names the cell beside it,
; an entry a word that is its own label or a label and its word, ("stopped at" stopped-at),
; told apart by list? (Frazaro's VLA.15). A verb writes its row at a word by at, which hands
; the word's sheet and cell in where the verb takes them: (at stop (rule ...)) is (rule
; "State" "B12" ...). And devices names the device cells a cartridge reads, each word asked
; for a label of docs/SPEC.md sections 3.3 and 3.5, player 1's: (devices a mouse-left frame)
; for Input!B5, Input!B13 and Clock!B1. Two labels are other words, select-button for select,
; which VBA's Select refuses, and sheet-shown for sheet, a row's kind; a word no device has is
; written as a not-a-device row, which the load refuses by name. A word is never a macro's
; name nor one defined already, and a macro's parameter of the same word hides it.

(defmacro (names sheet first & entries)
  "A block of named cells. Each entry's label goes down a column from the first cell, and its word names the cell beside the label. An entry is a word that is its own label, or a label and its word."
  (each-index (row entry entries (row-expand first))
    (name-entry sheet row (column-expand first) entry)))

(defmacro (name-entry sheet row column entry)
  "One entry of a block: a word that is its own label, or a label and its word."
  (quote-if (list? entry)
    (label-and-name sheet row column (car entry) (car (cdr entry)))
    (label-and-name sheet row column (&expand entry) entry)))

(defmacro (label-and-name sheet row column label word)
  "A label in its cell, and a word for the cell beside it."
  (cell sheet (address-expand row column) label)
  (define word (ref sheet (address-expand row (+expand column 1)))))

(defmacro (at word call)
  "A verb's row at a word: the word's sheet and cell handed in after the verb's name, as on hands a sheet in."
  (quasiquote
    ((unquote (car call))
     (sheet-expand (unquote word))
     (range-expand (unquote word))
     (unquote-splicing (cdr call)))))

(defmacro (devices & words)
  "Names the device cells a cartridge reads. Each word is the label of a cell of player 1's Input rows or of the Clock."
  (each (word words)
    (device word)))

(defmacro (device word)
  "One device cell's word, found in the table of the Input sheet's rows for player 1 and the Clock's."
  (device-entry word
    (assoc-expand word
      (quote ((up Input!B1) (down Input!B2) (left Input!B3) (right Input!B4)
              (a Input!B5) (b Input!B6) (x Input!B7) (y Input!B8)
              (start Input!B9) (select-button Input!B10)
              (mouse-x Input!B11) (mouse-y Input!B12) (mouse-left Input!B13)
              (mouse-right Input!B14) (mouse-middle Input!B15) (mouse-wheel Input!B16)
              (key Input!B17) (code Input!B18) (sheet-shown Input!B19) (command Input!B20)
              (frame Clock!B1) (rate Clock!B2) (seed Clock!B3))))))

(defmacro (device-entry word entry)
  "The define a device's entry gives, or the word written as a not-a-device row when no device has it."
  (quote-if (null? entry)
    (not-a-device word)
    (define word (car (cdr entry)))))

; ---- the Palette (docs/SPEC.md section 3.2) ----------------------------------------------

(defmacro (palette & entries)
  "The Palette's sixteen rows. Each entry is a color and its name, and the entry's place in the list, counted from 0, is its index."
  (each-index (index (color name) entries 0)
    (palette-entry index color name)))

(defmacro (palette-entry index color name)
  "One Palette row: the index in column A, the color in column B, the name in column C."
  (cell "Palette" (address-expand (+expand index 1) 1) index)
  (cell "Palette" (address-expand (+expand index 1) 2) color)
  (cell "Palette" (address-expand (+expand index 1) 3) name))

(defmacro (cga-palette)
  "the CGA's sixteen in their own order, docs/SPEC.md section 3.2's table, a palette with a name"
  (palette                          ; the sixteen colors, index 0 first
    ("#000000" "black")             ; 0
    ("#0000AA" "blue")              ; 1
    ("#00AA00" "green")             ; 2
    ("#00AAAA" "cyan")              ; 3
    ("#AA0000" "red")               ; 4
    ("#AA00AA" "magenta")           ; 5
    ("#AA5500" "brown")             ; 6
    ("#AAAAAA" "light gray")        ; 7
    ("#555555" "dark gray")         ; 8
    ("#5555FF" "light blue")        ; 9
    ("#55FF55" "light green")       ; 10
    ("#55FFFF" "light cyan")        ; 11
    ("#FF5555" "light red")         ; 12
    ("#FF55FF" "light magenta")     ; 13
    ("#FFFF55" "yellow")            ; 14
    ("#FFFFFF" "white")))           ; 15

; ---- the looks (docs/SPEC.md section 7.3) ------------------------------------------------
; The grid's twin of the Palette: a look map, each value drawn through a format whose
; fill is a color, so that the grid draws a sheet's values as the plane draws its bytes
; (docs/SPEC.md decision 19). A fill is written as the record writes it, six hex digits and
; no #.

(defmacro (looks sheet & fills)
  "a sheet's look map from a list of fills: the value n drawn through the format n+1, its fill the nth, from 0"
  (each-index (index fill fills 0)
    (look-entry sheet index fill)))

(defmacro (look-entry sheet index fill)
  "one fill of a look map: the format index+1 of the fill, and the value index drawn through it"
  (format (+expand index 1) fill general nowrap)
  (look sheet index (+expand index 1)))

; ---- the buttons and the keys (docs/SPEC.md sections 3.3 and 3.4) --------------------------

(defmacro (button-labels sheet)
  "the Input sheet's ten button labels in a sheet's column A, up to select, rows 1 to 10"
  (labels sheet "A1" "up" "down" "left" "right" "a" "b" "x" "y" "start" "select"))

(defmacro (keys letter & codes)
  "a player's column of the Keys sheet: the KeyboardEvent.code that holds each button, up to select, from row 1; the column's letter joined to the row"
  (each-index (row code codes 1)
    (cell "Keys" (&expand letter row) code)))

(defmacro (default-keys)
  "the Keys sheet as docs/SPEC.md section 3.4 tabulates it: the ten labels in column A, and player 1's keys, TIC-80's, in column B; a later player is a keys call"
  (button-labels "Keys")
  (keys "B"                         ; player 1: docs/SPEC.md section 3.4's defaults, TIC-80's
    "ArrowUp"                       ; up
    "ArrowDown"                     ; down
    "ArrowLeft"                     ; left
    "ArrowRight"                    ; right
    "KeyZ"                          ; a
    "KeyX"                          ; b
    "KeyA"                          ; x
    "KeyS"                          ; y
    "Enter"                         ; start
    "Space"))                       ; select

; ---- the Audio sheet (docs/SPEC.md section 3.6) ------------------------------------------
; A table, a voice a row: the header in row 1 and the voices' numbers in column A, rows 2
; to 5; a cartridge writes each voice's wave, note and volume in columns B to D itself.

(defmacro (audio)
  "the Audio sheet's header row, voice, wave, note and volume, and its four voices' numbers"
  (headers "Audio" "A1" "voice" "wave" "note" "volume")
  (labels "Audio" "A2" 1 2 3 4))

; ---- the Camera (docs/SPEC.md section 3.8) -----------------------------------------------
; Two cells the host places the Screen's window by, each beside its label. A still
; Camera holds two values, which only a person's edit moves; with a Camera, the Screen
; may hold cells beyond the window, which the plane never draws and a grid of the
; sheet does. A Camera that pans holds a formula, and is written as rows.

(defmacro (camera top left)
  "a still Camera: the window's top row and left column as values, each beside its label"
  (cell "Camera" "A1" "row")
  (cell "Camera" "B1" top)
  (cell "Camera" "A2" "column")
  (cell "Camera" "B2" left))

; ---- the Write sheet (docs/SPEC.md section 3.9) ------------------------------------------
; A row a write, from its cell in column A: the sheet a value goes to; in column B its
; address, or a range every cell of which takes the value, while a test holds, and
; else empty, which writes nothing; in column C the value. After each step the host
; issues each row as a derived write before the next frame, so a value lands a frame
; late. The table's header is the headers macro's, and put's pieces are its words:
; (put "A2" (sheet "Tally") (when (edge Input!B13)) (address "B20") (value Clock!B1)),
; the four in any order, each required. The test, the address and the value are
; expressions: an address that is one cell is a text, "B20", and one computed is a text
; joined by &, (& State!B30 State!B23). The Write sheet is put's first parameter, which
; on names once, and it is write-sheet, since the piece sheet takes that word.

(defmacro (put write-sheet at (sheet) (when) (address) (value))
  "a row of the Write sheet from its cell in column A, its pieces named: the sheet a value goes to; =IF(when,address,\"\"); =value"
  (cell write-sheet at sheet)
  (formula write-sheet (beside at 1) (formula-expand (if when address "")))
  (formula write-sheet (beside at 2) (formula-expand value)))

(defmacro (beside at columns)
  "the cell a number of columns to the right of a cell, as a text: C2 two beside A2"
  (address-expand (row-expand at) (+expand (column-expand at) columns)))

; ---- the verbs: first frame, interior, press, count, hold, dice, every, since ---------
; Each verb writes one formula row, one shape filled over a range, which the language
; computes as a run (docs/SPEC.md section 2's rules). The sheet comes first, so that on names
; it once, then the range, then what the verb means, in the order its formula reads it.
; Its other arguments are expressions, a reference, a test or a sum, written as the
; range's first cell reads them; the fill moves them as it moves every relative
; reference, and the formula syntax writes the row's text (KIT.5). A piece may be a
; macro's call, since the syntax expands its expression first: a verb's predicates can
; be named, and every pattern's value is still a cell a person sees, one verb writing a
; cell that another reads. A verb that reads its own last value writes the twin of its
; range's first cell, Tally.last!B1 for a fill over Tally!B1:E10, by its-last, the formula
; syntax's last over the range's first cell; and pressed writes its button's twin by last.
; Each reads its sheet and range only where the formula reads them, so a verb stands at a
; name, (at games (count start)), as it stands at an address.

(defmacro (first-frame sheet range start rule)
  "the first frame's value, then the rule every later frame: =IF(Clock!$B$1=1,start,rule)"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (if (= Clock!$B$1 1) start rule))))

; A board's interior (ENGINE.9): first-frame over every cell of a board but its border,
; one cell wide, which stays empty and reads as 0. The board's size comes first, its
; width and its height in cells, and not the sheet, so that a source states its board
; once, as a parameter that hands the size on: (board-size interior sheet start rule)
; becomes (interior 320 200 sheet start rule). A door builds the source on a larger board
; by handing the pass a later definition of the parameter (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8), and the
; same rule covers it. Its sheet is no first argument, so on cannot name it.

(defmacro (interior width height sheet start rule)
  "first-frame over a board width by height cells, less its border: B2 to the cell before its last row and column"
  (quasiquote (first-frame (unquote sheet) (unquote (&expand "B2:" (address-expand (-expand height 1) (-expand width 1)))) (unquote start) (unquote rule))))

(defmacro (edge button)
  "A button's rising edge, as a test any piece may hold: its cell is 1 this frame and was 0 the last, AND(button=1,its twin=0)."
  (and (= button 1) (= (last button) 0)))

(defmacro (pressed sheet range button)
  "1 in the frame a button goes down and 0 otherwise, its rising edge (docs/SPEC.md section 3.3): =IF(AND(button=1,its twin=0),1,0)"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (if (edge button) 1 0))))

(defmacro (its-last sheet range)
  "The last frame's value of a range's first cell, as the fill's first cell reads it: Tally.last!B1 for Tally!B1:E10."
  (last (ref sheet (first-cell-expand (ref sheet range)))))

(defmacro (count sheet range event)
  "each cell its own last value plus an event, a count of the frames it is 1 or a sum of its numbers: =sheet.last!first+event"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (+ (its-last sheet range) event))))

(defmacro (hold sheet range when new)
  "each cell its own last value until an event replaces it, docs/SPEC.md section 3.9's keep-last: =IF(when,new,sheet.last!first)"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (if when new (its-last sheet range)))))

(defmacro (dice sheet at)
  "Park and Miller's minimal standard in one cell (docs/SPEC.md section 3.5): the seed in the first frame, then the last value times 16807, modulo 2147483647; one cell, since its Clock references are relative and a fill would move them"
  (formula sheet at (formula-expand (if (= Clock!B1 1) Clock!B3 (mod (* (its-last sheet at) 16807) 2147483647)))))

(defmacro (every sheet range counted n)
  "1 in every nth frame of a count and 0 in the others, the clock divider of docs/SPEC.md section 12 over any count: =IF(MOD(count,n)=0,1,0)"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (if (= (mod counted n) 0) 1 0))))

(defmacro (since sheet range event)
  "the frames since an event, 0 in its frame and one more in each frame after, Appendix C's age: =IF(event,0,sheet.last!first+1)"
  (formula sheet range (formula-expand (if event 0 (+ (its-last sheet range) 1)))))

; ---- the expressions a piece may hold: within, priority (KIT.6) -----------------------
; Each stands inside any piece, as edge does, and writes what a person writes in Excel by
; hand: within a test of two bounds, both included, and priority a choice by the first
; test that holds, the nested IFs that Excel's IFS would be, which the language's library
; does not hold. A priority's clauses are a list, each a test and its value and (else
; value) the last, so that a choice of five reads as five lines; with no else it answers
; #N/A, as IFS does when no test holds. A test may be any expression, a bare reference
; among them, and an else is found by equal?, since eq? refuses a list. A within inside
; an and is an AND of its own, (and a (within x 1 3)) writing AND(a,AND(x>=1,x<=3)): the
; same test, and other bytes than one flat AND, which a rewrite that keeps a cartridge's
; bytes keeps as it was.

(defmacro (within x low high)
  "x between two bounds, both included, as a test: AND(x>=low,x<=high)"
  (and (>= x low) (<= x high)))

(defmacro (priority & clauses)
  "a choice by the first test that holds, as nested IFs: each clause a test and its value, the last (else value); #N/A with no else, as IFS answers"
  (quote-if (null? clauses)
    (error "#N/A")
    (quote-if (equal? (car (car clauses)) else)
      (car (cdr (car clauses)))
      (if (car (car clauses))
          (car (cdr (car clauses)))
          (quasiquote (priority (unquote-splicing (cdr clauses))))))))

; ---- pictures -----------------------------------------------------------------------
; A picture is rows of text: each string one row of cells, down from a top-left cell,
; and each character one cell, its value the legend's, so that a sprite, a tile or a
; pattern is written as it looks. A dot writes no cell, in every legend, so a picture's
; empty cells are no rows at all, which the plane reads as 0 (docs/SPEC.md section 3.1); a
; legend's entry for a dot is never read, and a space is a character like any other. A
; row shorter than another writes nothing past its end. The legend is hex, PICO-8's
; sixteen digits, 0 to 9 and a to f the Palette's indices 0 to 15, as a PICO-8
; cartridge keeps its sprites; or a list of entries, each a character and its value, a
; number, a text or a truth value, the first entry for a character giving its value:
; (("O" 1)) for a Life pattern, O a live cell. A legend's key is a character, a text,
; ("7" true) and never (7 true), since an entry is found by its head as written. A
; character the legend does not hold writes a row the load refuses, (not-in-the-legend
; sheet cell character), where its cell would be, so that the cartridge says where. A
; picture writes a row a cell and never a range, so a block of one value is a cells
; entry. Its rows and their characters are two loops, one application each, so a
; picture holds as many rows and cells as its sheet does (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8).

(defmacro (picture sheet top-left legend & rows)
  "rows of cells drawn as text: each string a row down from the top-left, each character a cell, its value the legend's; a dot writes no cell; the legend hex, PICO-8's sixteen digits, or a list of (character value) entries"
  (each-index (row text rows (row-expand top-left))
    (each-index (column character (characters-expand text) (column-expand top-left))
      (picture-cell sheet (address-expand row column) character legend))))

(defmacro (picture-cell sheet at character legend)
  "one character's cell: a dot writes none, and any other its value in hex or in the legend's entries"
  (quote-if (eq? character ".")
    (begin)
    (quote-if (equal? legend hex)
      (picture-hex sheet at character)
      (picture-legend sheet at character legend))))

(defmacro (picture-hex sheet at character)
  "a character's cell in PICO-8's sixteen digits, 0 to 9 and a to f the Palette's indices 0 to 15, its clauses tried in one application; any other character a row the load refuses"
  (cond
    ((eq? character "0") (cell sheet at 0))
    ((eq? character "1") (cell sheet at 1))
    ((eq? character "2") (cell sheet at 2))
    ((eq? character "3") (cell sheet at 3))
    ((eq? character "4") (cell sheet at 4))
    ((eq? character "5") (cell sheet at 5))
    ((eq? character "6") (cell sheet at 6))
    ((eq? character "7") (cell sheet at 7))
    ((eq? character "8") (cell sheet at 8))
    ((eq? character "9") (cell sheet at 9))
    ((eq? character "a") (cell sheet at 10))
    ((eq? character "b") (cell sheet at 11))
    ((eq? character "c") (cell sheet at 12))
    ((eq? character "d") (cell sheet at 13))
    ((eq? character "e") (cell sheet at 14))
    ((eq? character "f") (cell sheet at 15))
    (else (not-in-the-legend sheet at character))))

(defmacro (picture-legend sheet at character legend)
  "a character's cell in a legend of (character value) entries, the first whose key is the character giving its value; a character none holds a row the load refuses"
  (quote-if (null? (assoc-expand character legend))
    (not-in-the-legend sheet at character)
    (cell sheet at (car (cdr (assoc-expand character legend))))))
